# Generated theme output (D-14) — matugen rewrites these on every wallpaper or
# colour-scheme change, so tracking them means a diff per wallpaper. PROJECT.md
# already excludes kdeglobals, Kvantum/ and both gtk.css siblings by hand;
# these patterns make that exclusion mechanical.
#
# Slash-free ON PURPOSE. A gitignore pattern with no slash, or with a slash only
# at the end, matches at ANY depth — which is exactly the semantics these need,
# because the same generated file appears at the repo root (.config/kdeglobals),
# under stow/<pkg>/.config/, and under any future restow/ tree. Do NOT rewrite
# them as .config/<path>: a pattern with a non-trailing slash is anchored to the
# directory holding this file (the repo root), which is why the two patterns at
# the top of this file reach nothing.
#
# .config/kdeglobals is already TRACKED, and a gitignore line never untracks a
# tracked file. This pattern governs future writes only; the untracking is a
# Phase 18 redistribution decision under FIX-03 and is handed off, not taken here.
kdeglobals
gtk.css
Kvantum/
colors.lua
colors.conf
fuzzel_theme.ini

# Machine-written state (D-14) — caches, virtualenvs, editor droppings, runtime
# sockets and lockfiles. Same anchoring rule as the block above: slash-free
# means any depth, and anything that belongs to ONE package must instead be
# written fully qualified from the repo root, like the qBittorrent block.
#
# Per-tree ignore rules are deliberately absent: they need Phase 18's collision
# map to say which tree a path belongs to (D-14).
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
*.sock
*.socket
*.lock
